{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'codex exec --help'","aggregated_output":"WARNING: failed to clean up stale arg0 temp dirs: 拒绝访问。 (os error 5)\nWARNING: proceeding, even though we could not create PATH aliases: 拒绝访问。 (os error 5) at path \"C:\\\\Users\\\\EDY\\\\.codex\\\\tmp\\\\arg0-windows\\\\codex-arg0gKkMF8\"\nRun Codex non-interactively\n\nUsage: codex exec [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]\n       codex exec [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGS]\n\nCommands:\n  resume  Resume a previous session by id or pick the most recent with --last\n  fork    Fork a previous session by id into a new session\n  review  Run a code review against the current repository\n  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nArguments:\n  [PROMPT]\n          Initial instructions for the agent. If not provided as an argument (or if `-` is used),\n          instructions are read from stdin. If stdin is piped and a prompt is also provided, stdin\n          is appended as a `<stdin>` block\n\nOptions:\n  -c, --config <key=value>\n          Override a configuration value that would otherwise be loaded from `~/.codex/config.toml`.\n          Use a dotted path (`foo.bar.baz`) to override nested values. The `value` portion is parsed\n          as TOML. If it fails to parse as TOML, the raw string is used as a literal.\n          \n          Examples: - `-c model=\"o3\"` - `-c 'sandbox_permissions=[\"disk-full-read-access\"]'` - `-c\n          shell_environment_policy.inherit=all`\n\n      --enable <FEATURE>\n          Enable a feature (repeatable). Equivalent to `-c features.<name>=true`\n\n      --disable <FEATURE>\n          Disable a feature (repeatable). Equivalent to `-c features.<name>=false`\n\n      --strict-config\n          Error out when config.toml contains fields that are not recognized by this version of\n          Codex\n\n  -i, --image <FILE>...\n          Optional image(s) to attach to the initial prompt\n\n  -m, --model <MODEL>\n          Model the agent should use\n\n      --oss\n          Use open-source provider\n\n      --local-provider <OSS_PROVIDER>\n          Specify which local provider to use (lmstudio or ollama). If not specified with --oss,\n          will use config default or show selection\n\n  -p, --profile <CONFIG_PROFILE_V2>\n          Layer $CODEX_HOME/<name>.config.toml on top of the base user config\n\n  -s, --sandbox <SANDBOX_MODE>\n          Select the sandbox policy to use when executing model-generated shell commands\n          \n          [possible values: read-only, workspace-write, danger-full-access]\n\n      --approve-for-me\n          Route approval requests through automatic review using the workspace-write sandbox\n\n      --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\n          Skip all confirmation prompts and execute commands without sandboxing. EXTREMELY\n          DANGEROUS. Intended solely for running in environments that are externally sandboxed\n\n      --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust\n          Run enabled hooks without requiring persisted hook trust for this invocation. DANGEROUS.\n          Intended only for automation that already vets hook sources\n\n  -C, --cd <DIR>\n          Tell the agent to use the specified directory as its working root\n\n      --worktree\n          Run the session in a new managed Git worktree\n\n      --add-dir <DIR>\n          Additional directories that should be writable alongside the primary workspace\n\n      --thread-source <SOURCE>\n          Source classification for newly created or forked threads\n\n      --cyber-access-program <PROGRAM>\n          Request an experimental Cyber access program for this turn (OpenAI provider only). Omit to\n          use server defaults. Not supported with review; fork requires a prompt\n          \n          [possible values: standard, daybreak_blue, daybreak_red]\n\n      --skip-git-repo-check\n          Allow running Codex outside a Git repository\n\n      --ephemeral\n          Run without persisting session files to disk\n\n      --ignore-user-config\n          Do not load `$CODEX_HOME/config.toml`; auth still uses `CODEX_HOME`\n\n      --ignore-rules\n          Do not load user or project execpolicy `.rules` files\n\n      --output-schema <FILE>\n          Path to a JSON Schema file describing the model's final response shape\n\n      --color <COLOR>\n          Specifies color settings for use in the output\n          \n          [default: auto]\n          [possible values: always, never, auto]\n\n      --json\n          Print events to stdout as JSONL\n\n  -o, --output-last-message <FILE>\n          Specifies file where the last message from the agent should be written\n\n  -h, --help\n          Print help (see a summary with '-h')\n\n  -V, --version\n          Print version\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"overall_quality\": \"不通过。R2 已补充独立盲区快照、工作目录和输出判定优先级，但上一轮关于事件流、预算持久化、失败分类和临时文件唯一性的问题仍未完全闭合。方案自身声称已补充 --json，实际命令却未包含该参数，影响用量记录和验收。\",\n  \"score\": 7.4,\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"location\": \"方案第 2.2、2.4 和 4 节，第 41—45、62—63、102—104 行\",\n      \"problem\": \"调用模板没有 --json，却将标准输出保存为 .jsonl 并要求从中解析事件、用量和实际模型。标题中的 R2 修订说明声称已补充 --json，与实际模板不符。\",\n      \"evidence\": \"本机 codex exec --help 明确说明 --json 才会向标准输出打印 JSONL 事件；现有模板仅重定向标准输出。\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"在模板中加入 --json，明确解析所需事件与字段；字段缺失时记录不可验证，并让正常路径验收检查实际事件流。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"location\": \"方案第 2.3 节，第 53、57 行\",\n      \"problem\": \"台账写入失败时仍允许调用，与单任务 2 次硬上限冲突。此次调用无法持久化计数，后续轮次或上下文压缩后可能再次启动，超过预算。台账按任务关键词命名，也未定义同名任务如何区分及恢复时如何确定正确台账。\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"明确唯一任务标识、台账创建与恢复规则；启动前检查并持久化扣次，持久化失败时停止调用或采用能够可靠维持预算的替代机制。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"location\": \"方案第 2.3、2.5 节，第 57、70—72 行\",\n      \"problem\": \"失败分类仍未完整闭合。模型或强度不支持均回落到同一模型的 high；如果模型名称本身不可用，回落强度无法解决问题。重试再次出现同类错误后的处理未定义，且该行只写“重试扣次”，没有像进程失败一样明确首次启动也扣次。\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"区分模型不可用与强度不支持；规定首次启动和每次重试均扣次、重试前检查预算，以及回落仍失败后的最终降级和是否禁用。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"location\": \"方案第 2.1 节，第 31—33 行\",\n      \"problem\": \"时间戳精确到秒且仅附两位随机值，不能保证每次尝试唯一；方案也未规定发生碰撞时如何避免覆盖。固定台账名称同样可能与其他同关键词任务冲突。\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"使用足够随机的标识并以排他方式创建文件，碰撞时重新生成；台账使用独立任务标识并明确恢复映射。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"location\": \"方案第 2.3 节，第 55—56 行\",\n      \"problem\": \"盲区扫描复用要求至少一条 Markdown 列表项的合并判定，但其提示词只要求输出最多 5 条洞察，没有要求列表格式；正常回答若采用段落或标题格式会被判为解析失败。\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"在盲区扫描提示词中明确输出 Markdown 列表，或为该路径定义对应的可验证解析规则。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"location\": \"方案第 2.1、2.3 和 4 节，第 31、53、102 行\",\n      \"problem\": \"台账和日志的归属未完全统一：通用临时目录以“日志所在目录”为基准，但 pacemaker 只定义当前目录的台账；验收又要求 brainstorm 的台账记录模型与用量，而 brainstorm 仅定义了思考日志状态行。\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"分别明确两种技能的工作目录、记录载体和模型用量写入位置，使模板、清理规则及验收引用同一载体。\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"suggestions\": [\n    \"上一轮第 1 项未解决：模板仍缺少 --json；实际生效值与请求值的区分原则已写明，但需要可用的证据来源。\",\n    \"上一轮第 2 项部分解决：已新增 pacemaker 台账，但写入失败后继续调用及台账定位规则仍会削弱预算上限。\",\n    \"上一轮第 3 项部分解决：已增加分类表和重试前预算检查，但模型不可用与强度不可用的处理仍需拆开，首次扣次及再次失败后的行为需明确。\",\n    \"上一轮第 4 项已解决：盲区扫描使用不包含宿主洞察和论证的独立快照。\",\n    \"上一轮第 5 项部分解决：已禁止清理非本次文件，但当前 ID 生成方式及创建规则仍不能保证不发生碰撞或覆盖。\",\n    \"上一轮第 6 项基本解决：模板已显式指定 -C，并对工作目录和输出路径加引号；仍应按第 106 行用含空格及非 Git 目录验证实际调用。\",\n    \"上一轮第 7 项基本解决：已规定仅在退出码为 0 且输出符合条件时合并，失败或中断时忽略部分输出，并记录清理失败；建议将超时和中断加入验收。\"\n  ]\n}"}}
